// B1 course (A2 → B1 roadmap), module 16 „Arvamus, võrdlemine ja põhjendamine” (a2b1-076…080), stage B1.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline: a week of arguments in the course's world
// — the Mets family about Oskar's phone, Sofia's office (Tuul Logistika) about remote work, Jaan's house about its
// courtyard — and one goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner takes part in the residents' meeting, helps it
// reach a decision (Harno B1 speaking: reach an agreement) and writes an opinion text for the house (079 Kasuta).
// Topics the B1 course lacked: media and technology (children's screen time, phones at school, e-Estonia services,
// remote work) and society / current events (a news study, a city poll on 30 km/h, the participatory budget).
// No new grammar item; the module consolidates the B1 items met earlier: opinion phrases with the verb second and
// sest / kuna (076), comparison — keskvõrre + kui, sama … kui, nagu, kõige, võrreldes + -ga (077), argument words
// seepärast / seetõttu / seega / näiteks with kes / mis relative clauses (078), the conditional for a polite opinion —
// ma arvaksin, oleks parem, võiksime (079). Module 15's words (eesmärk, plaan, otsustama, saavutama, variant…) return.
//   076 the Mets kitchen: Oskar wants a smartphone (listening), a news study on screen time; the parents' forum, Oskar's
//       plan; Kase kool proposes a phone locker — the parents' meeting and a letter to the class teacher.
//   077 Sofia's blog: two weeks at home and in the office, her colleagues' cards; a radio programme on e-Estonia with
//       Viktor, his letter to Helgi; Liis asks for a remote-work rule — the team talk, the proposal to Liis.
//   078 Jaan's house group: playground or parking? the city's participatory budget; Urmas's article, the radio news on
//       30 km/h; a call-in programme — the caller's speech and a comment on the programme's page.
//   079 a radio debate on courtyards, advice on reaching agreement; Kadri and Karl on the stairs, another house's
//       minutes, the family decides Oskar's phone rules; the residents' meeting — a decision and an opinion text.
// Lesson 5 (080) is the module's assessment in Harno B1 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b1/module16.js,
